Package: strawberry-video-player
Version: 2.7.5
Section: video
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: mpv, ffmpeg, vlc-bin, vlc-plugin-base, python3 (>= 3.9), python3-evdev, python3-pil, pulseaudio-utils | pipewire-pulse
Recommends: polkitd | policykit-1, fonts-dejavu-core, kms++-utils
Maintainer: dave-taylor-7654 <167921850+dave-taylor-7654@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: Offline video player, HDMI diagnostics and test patterns for AV professionals
 Plays the videos in ~/Videos in alphabetical order, looping, on HDMI when a
 display is connected and otherwise on the built-in LCD, with sound following
 the picture. Press i for HDMI diagnostics on the LCD (the display's name, the
 active mode, color range, audio formats, link status and CEC address) and t for
 test patterns (color bars, gray steps, geometry, convergence, audio and sync).
 Keyboard: Tab LCD/HDMI, q/Space play-pause, z/x previous, c/f next, w/e skip
 30 s, s/d volume, a mute, l loop, 1-8 aspect ratio, i HDMI diagnostics,
 t test patterns, h help, Esc quit.
 .
 On HDMI the player can use VLC's hardware DRM output for smooth 1080p. That
 needs permission to stop the desktop while playing; without it, HDMI plays in
 a window on the desktop instead.
